35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the treasurer’s hours. Chasing money for individual sessions took six hours a month, but yearly collection took barely one.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, billed regardless of attendance. The bank statements confirm a third of renewals required reminders. We cannot rely on consistent cash flow.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The sign-in sheets show a quarter of members account for two-thirds of attendances, with eighteen names absent entirely. The taster forms reveal nine of fourteen non-joiners refused a whole-year commitment.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The data is damning. A door charge killed weekday turnout by a third. Plus, quiet members dread the per-event math. We need a structure that feels like belonging, not a transaction.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The sign-in sheets confirm my suspicion. A quarter of members do two-thirds of the work, while eighteen pay but never show. The rota proves the same nine people carry the physical load.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I’m relieved. If yearly collection is easier, maybe we can choose that. It would be much kinder to the next treasurer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, the administrative ease is noted. However, with seventy percent of costs fixed and a third of income delayed, a flat fee risks cash flow gaps. We need certainty.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, certainty is good, but the taster forms show people reject the whole-year commitment. We need a structure that welcomes drifters without breaking the core group.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, I hear you, but the data says people stop feeling ownership when they pay per event. We need a fee that feels like a home, not a ticket.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the data proves the core group is already carrying the weight. A flat fee just subsidizes the eighteen ghosts. We need to address the imbalance, not hide it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I worry about the eighteen people who never come. If they pay the same, is that fair to the busy ones?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Shunichi, the ledger proves those fixed costs exist regardless of attendance. A flat fee is the only way to guarantee we cover them without chasing individuals.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, the imbalance is real, but the taster forms show a whole-year commitment scares people away. We need a structure that welcomes drifters without breaking the core group.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you’re focusing on the wrong problem. The ghosts aren’t the issue; the hesitation is. If we make membership feel like a burden, we lose the people who actually show up.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the ghosts are the issue. They pay for a service they never use. We need to stop subsidizing absence.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want the books to be simple. If a flat fee means less chasing, I am for it.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, simplicity is not the only metric. We must balance administrative ease with financial security. The fixed costs demand a reliable, upfront income stream to prevent gaps.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, I hear the need for security. But the taster forms show a whole-year commitment scares people away. We need a structure that welcomes drifters without breaking the core group.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minako, the taster forms show fear of commitment, not a desire for tiers. A flat fee is the only way to make belonging feel automatic, not a calculation.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the taster forms show fear of commitment, not a desire for tiers. A flat fee is the only way to make belonging feel automatic, not a calculation.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
